text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Fraysseix and Rosenstiehl, in Brandes’s formulation, 2009); "},{"code":"findKuratowskiSubgraph()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" runs"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Boyer and Myrvold’s edge-addition algorithm (2004), whose failure state isolates the witness."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"All are O(n + m), iterative, and deterministic: graphs with the same rows (the same vertices in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the same order, the same edge positions, the same incidence order) get the same embedding and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the same witness."}]}]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/planarity\/graphprotocols\/graph"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Planarity\/documentation\/Planarity","doc:\/\/Planarity\/documentation\/Planarity\/GraphProtocols"]]},"abstract":[{"text":"Planarity on undirected graphs. Self-loops and parallel edges never change an answer: the tests","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"run on the underlying simple graph, read once through the rows in index space. A directed","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"graph’s planarity is that of ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"graph.undirected"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"references":{"doc://Planarity/documentation/Planarity":{"role":"collection","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/planarity","title":"Planarity","abstract":[],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Planarity\/documentation\/Planarity"},"doc://Planarity/documentation/Planarity/GraphProtocols/Graph/planarEmbedding()":{"title":"planarEmbedding()","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Planarity\/documentation\/Planarity\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/planarEmbedding()","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"planarEmbedding"},{"k